        ],
        "answer": "[01_regression.md#3.0] (01_regression.md) Regularization, specifically L2 (Ridge) and L1 (Lasso) penalties, keep statistical models from memorizing empirical training noise by penalizing model complexity in the loss objective. L2 Regularization adds the squared Euclidean norm of weights (lambda * ||w||_2^2), and L1 Regularization penalizes absolute weight magnitudes (lambda * ||w||_1). This penalization drives coefficient magnitudes toward zero, reducing the model's complexity and preventing it from overfitting to the training data's noise.",
